{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HOS",
  "chapter": 11,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Israel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a child, then I loved him, and called my son out of Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they called them, so they went from them: they sacrificed to Baalim, and burned incense to graven images.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I taught Ephraim also to go, taking them by their arms; but they knew not that I healed them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I drew them with cords of a man, with bands of love: and I was to them as they that take off the yoke on their jaws, and I laid food for them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall not return into the land of Egypt, but the Assyrian shall be his king, because they refused to return.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the sword shall abide on his cities, and shall consume his branches, and devour ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", because of their own counsels.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And my people are bent to backsliding from me: though they called them to the most High, none at all would exalt ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How shall I give thee up, Ephraim? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "how",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall I deliver thee, Israel? how shall I make thee as Admah? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "how",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall I set thee as Zeboim? my heart is turned within me, my repentings are kindled together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will not execute the fierceness of my anger, I will not return to destroy Ephraim: for I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God, and not man; the Holy One in the midst of thee: and I will not enter into the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall walk after the LORD: he shall roar like a lion: when he shall roar, then the children shall tremble from the west.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall tremble as a bird out of Egypt, and as a dove out of the land of Assyria: and I will place them in their houses, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.11.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.11.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ephraim encompasseth me with lies, and the house of Israel with deceit: but Judah yet ruleth with God, and is faithful with the saints.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
